    <decisions>
        <name>Opportunity_Not_Already_Closed</name>
        <label>Opportunity Not Already Closed?</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>50</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Get_Owner_User_ForEmail</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Already Closed - Do Nothing</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Not_Closed</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Opportunity_ForClose.StageName</leftValueReference>
                <operator>NotEqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Closed Won</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Opportunity_ForClose.StageName</leftValueReference>
                <operator>NotEqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Closed Lost</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Update_Opportunity_Closed</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Not Already Closed</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Fires when AF_ApprovalStatus__c changes to Approved. Notifies the Credit Note Owner via email and Custom Notification - same dual-channel pattern as AF_FL_Reservation_Approved.

LFRDN-725 fix: this flow only ever notified - approving a cancellation&apos;s Credit Note never closed the related Opportunity, leaving a cancelled deal sitting open indefinitely. Added Update_Opportunity_Closed, setting StageName to Closed Lost (the only closed-and-not-won stage this org&apos;s Stage picklist has - there is no dedicated Cancelled stage) whenever the Opportunity isn&apos;t already closed. Does not set AF_LostReason__c - none of its existing values describe a post-sale cancellation cleanly, and per this org&apos;s standing practice, business-specific picklist data is left to the reporter/BA rather than guessed.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>AF_Formula_Subject</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;Approved: Cancellation/Refund &quot; &amp; {!$Record.Name}</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>NotifBody</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;Your cancellation/refund request &quot; &amp; {!$Record.Name} &amp; &quot; was approved.&quot;</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>NotifTitle</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;Cancellation/Refund Approved: &quot; &amp; {!$Record.Name}</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>Credit Note Approved {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Credit Note Approved</label>
